From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:47:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] serve: background admissions and priority finishes
 (opt-in STRATA_SERVER_READS=1)

An admission with STRATA_READS_BG_MIN new tokens or more (default 8192) on an engine with INFO reads names a reserved
top-row slot (bg=<park>); after BREAD the control lines and the admission slot go back, the request waits on the park
slot's lines (BPP, BREADY, BRDONE), then takes the lines before every other waiting request and finishes with
yslot=<park> (or in the park slot itself).  BRDONE err: read again on the lines without bg=; a client that leaves
meanwhile BSTOPs the read and frees the park slot at its BRDONE.  serve/test_reads.py with a fake engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
