+# its BGEN names a free top-row slot (bg=<park>, reserved here: its own slot when that is one); the engine copies the part
+# read so far there and ends the request (BREAD <slot> <park> <q>, DONE cancel, BADM 0), reads the rest between its
+# lines while the slots decode and other admissions come and go (BPP <park> ... progress), then says BREADY <park> <h>.
